WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:07.145
"Naturally Boosting AMPK
with Exercise for Life Extension" 

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:10.160
How can we naturally boost
the enzyme AMPK

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:13.520
to slow aging
without starving ourselves?

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:17.480
AMPK is activated
by a fuel shortage.

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:19.320
If we don't want to limit
the amount of energy

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:20.920
going in through our mouths,

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:22.800
then we have to ramp up
the amount of energy

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:25.240
going out through our muscles.

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:28.320
Put people on a bike and start
taking muscle biopsies

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:29.240
while they cycle,

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:32.400
and you can detect a near
tripling of AMPK activation

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:34.320
within twenty minutes

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:36.880
in both diabetics
and nondiabetics.

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:38.520
That makes sense.

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:41.440
The muscles use up
the ATP to contract,

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:45.440
so AMP builds up
and AMPK is activated.

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:49.400
That may be one of the ways
exercise leads to weight loss.

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:54.680
AMPK activation also leads
to mitochondrial biogenesis,

00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:57.680
meaning the formation
of extra mitochondria,

00:00:57.680 --> 00:00:59.680
the power plants
within our cells

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:02.840
where fat is burned
and ATP is created.

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:05.400
So, AMPK doesn't
just cause more fat

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:07.560
to be shoveled
into the furnace,

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:10.600
it also causes more furnaces
to be built.

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:14.200
In this way, AMPK helps explain
why endurance training

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:17.600
eventually enables us
to run faster and farther.

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:19.600
So, might an AMPK activator

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:22.960
be like
the fabled exercise-in-a-pill?

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:24.680
Indeed, AMPK activation

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:27.600
can dramatically enhance
performance.

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:31.040
An AMPK-activator drug given
to sedentary mice for a month

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:34.560
boosted their running endurance
by 44 percent.

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:36.400
After one such drug
was discovered

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:38.320
at the famed Tour de France,

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:40.280
AMPK activators were banned

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:42.680
by the World Anti-Doping Agency.

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:47.280
So not just fasting in a pill,
but an exercise mimetic too?

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:49.720
People are often
"unwilling to perform

00:01:49.720 --> 00:01:51.760
even a minimum
of physical activity..."

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:53.360
wrote a group
of pharmacologists,

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:56.200
"thus, indicating that drugs
mimicking endurance exercise

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:58.360
are highly desirable."

00:01:58.360 --> 00:02:03.360
The "mass appeal" of such a drug
may tempt "big pharma"

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:05.320
to view physical inactivity

00:02:05.320 --> 00:02:08.360
as a market to be medicalized
for profit."

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:10.520
But that vision
pales in comparison

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:14.880
to the universal market
for an anti-aging remedy.

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:18.040
In his essay
"On youth and old age,"

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:20.200
the Greek philosopher Aristotle

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:24.160
described death
as the loss of inner heat.

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:26.400
Indeed, the progressive loss
of function

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:29.800
of the estimated 10 million
billion mitochondria

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:32.960
spread throughout the body
is considered a core tenet

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:34.520
of the biology of aging,

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:36.600
but mitochondrial dysfunction

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:38.400
isn't just a consequence
of aging,

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:40.960
but one of its causes.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:44.640
Dysfunctional mitochondria are
thought to actively contribute

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:45.880
to the aging process,

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:48.960
an insight illustrated
by a pioneering experiment

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:51.840
published over 30 years ago.

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:54.440
If you inject mitochondria
from a young animal

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:56.880
into a human cell,
nothing happens.

00:02:56.880 --> 00:02:58.840
The cell doesn't appear
to notice.

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:02.480
Human skin cells average
about 300 mitochondria each,

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:04.840
and adding 10 to 15 extras
from a young rat

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:06.960
didn't appear
to have any effect.

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:10.800
But add the same number
of mitochondria from an old rat,

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:14.280
and the human cells start
showing signs of degeneration

00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:16.200
within just a few days.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:19.360
Even just having a few percent
of those old mitochondria

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:20.840
was enough to drive
the human cells

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:22.640
to an early grave.

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:24.560
So, age-impaired mitochondria

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:26.640
don't just become
less efficient,

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:29.240
but may become actively harmful.

00:03:29.240 --> 00:03:33.680
So, if centenarian-equivalent
rat mitochondria are so toxic,

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:37.040
how do centenarian
human cells survive?

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:38.640
A group of Italian researchers

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:42.920
took some centenarian
skin biopsies to find out.

00:03:42.920 --> 00:03:44.920
Skin samples
taken from the forearms

00:03:44.920 --> 00:03:45.960
of young individuals

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:48.760
were compared to those
of elderly individuals.

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:52.560
As expected, each mitochondrial
mite from the older cells

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:55.400
was comparatively defective,
less efficient,

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:57.320
leaking free radicals.

00:03:57.320 --> 00:03:58.680
But to the scientists' surprise,

00:03:58.680 --> 00:04:01.320
the total amount of ATP
the centenarian cells

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:03.400
were pumping out
was even greater

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:05.400
than that of the younger cells.

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:07.040
How is that possible?

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:10.520
Because of a bulked up
mitochondrial mass.

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:13.800
It's like if an older Mike Tyson
took on a featherweight.

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:15.440
Even if pound-for-pound

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:19.480
the whipper-snapper's biceps
were more energy-generating,

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:23.680
Mike's sheer muscular mass
might prevail.

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:27.400
So how did the centenarian
mitochondria get swole?

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:29.120
AMPK.

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:31.520
Mitochondria can take up
anywhere between 2 percent

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:33.760
and 50 percent
of the volume of a cell

00:04:33.760 --> 00:04:35.600
and are in constant motion,

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:37.360
merging together
and splitting apart

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:40.080
like the molten wax
of a lava lamp.

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:41.680
In times of starvation
or stress,

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:44.560
the fusing of individual
mitochondria together

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:47.840
into a large tubular network
can be advantageous,

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:49.120
in part by diluting
the effects

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:50.560
of damaged mitochondria

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:53.600
by mixing their contents
in with others.

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:55.960
AMPK appears to accomplish this

00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:59.960
by tipping the lava lamp balance
from fission to fusion

00:04:59.960 --> 00:05:01.360
by blocking
one of the proteins

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:03.920
necessary to break mitochondria
back apart.

00:05:03.920 --> 00:05:05.480
This is thought
to be one of the routes

00:05:05.480 --> 00:05:07.160
by which endurance exercise

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:09.640
can rejuvenate
mitochondrial function.

00:05:09.640 --> 00:05:11.480
Thanks to AMPK,

00:05:11.480 --> 00:05:14.520
working out may magnify
your mitochondria

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:17.520
as well as your muscles.

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:20.560
Our mitochondrial function
does decline with age,

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:22.880
in part through
the impaired ability of AMPK

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:24.880
to generate new mitochondria,

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:28.000
but AMPK can build
new cellular power plants,

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:30.800
expand existing ones,
and decommission old ones

00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:32.760
(so-called mitophagy).

00:05:32.760 --> 00:05:36.200
AMPK is said to serve
as a "mitochondrial guardian,"

00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:37.920
and in that role
may help guard against

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:40.720
the ravages
of age-related disease.

00:05:40.720 --> 00:05:43.640
If an AMPK activating drug
really could help us

00:05:43.640 --> 00:05:46.160
reap the fat-burning
and health-promoting benefits

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:49.360
of fasting and exercise
without the hunger and sweat,

00:05:49.360 --> 00:05:50.880
one could imagine
how it would become

00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:54.520
one of the best-selling drugs
on the planet.

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:57.120
And it is.

00:05:57.120 --> 00:05:59.920
It's called metformin,

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:02.240
prescribed more
than 90 million times a year

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:04.240
in the U.S. alone.

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:07.880
But should we all be taking it
to prolong our lives?

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:27.720
That's what
I'll be covering next.

